  "detailed_description": "The scheme &amp;quot;Atma Nirbhar Pashu Palan Yojna (ANPPY)&amp;quot;, implemented by the Department of Animal Husbandry, Veterinary &amp;amp; Dairy Development, Government of Arunachal Pradesh, aims to enhance rural livelihoods, promote sustainable animal husbandry practices, and contribute to self-reliance in the livestock sector. Under this scheme, financial assistance in the form of credit-linked support is provided to unemployed individuals, Self-Help Groups (SHGs), farmers&amp;#39; clubs, cooperative societies, and Dairy Cooperative Societies (DCS) for livestock rearing and allied activities.\n",
  "eligibility": "The following beneficiaries are eligible under this scheme:\n\n  - Arunachal State Rural Livelihoods Mission (ArSRLM) promoted Self-Help Groups (SHGs), individuals, Farmers&amp;#39; Clubs, Registered Cooperative Societies, and Dairy Cooperative Societies (DCS) will be eligible.\n  - Individuals should belong to the Arunachal Pradesh Scheduled Tribe (APST) category and be unemployed.\n\n",
  "exclusions": null,
